    <string name="dsh_setup_title">Set up DeepSeek Harness</string>
    <string name="dsh_setup_row_hint">Install, update or check it in Termux</string>
    <string name="dsh_setup_intro">DeepSeek Harness runs in Termux, inside a small Ubuntu system. This setup installs Ubuntu, Node.js and DeepSeek Harness there. It needs about 1.5 GB of free space, downloads several hundred MB and can take 10–30 minutes, so use Wi-Fi and keep the phone charging. You can leave this screen: the setup goes on in Termux.</string>
    <string name="termux_setup_row">Set up Linux commands</string>
    <string name="termux_row_allowed">Termux is installed and allowed. Tap to check or finish setting up.</string>
    <string name="termux_setup_intro">Lets the assistant run commands in Termux: look things up on the web (weather, news), work with data, write and test code. This works with every engine; DeepSeek Harness has its own setup on top.</string>
    <string name="termux_section_tools">Tools</string>
